{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKpKB3BRbKZNGAsSfUj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied in the working tree, but I haven't committed it. Commits are yours to make.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and dropped the remainder. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, which loses the 1 grosz.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): the first `total % people` people each get one extra grosz.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_remainder_is_not_lost` to `test_money.py` before the fix, following the project's TDD skill, which says hotfixes start with a failing test. It failed on `[33, 33, 33]`, then passed after the fix. All 4 tests pass.\n\nSpot checks: `split_cents(0, 4)` gives `[0, 0, 0, 0]`, `split_cents(7, 7)` gives seven 1s, and `split_cents(1001, 6)` sums back to 1001. The zero-people `ValueError` is unchanged.\n\nThe test is about 4 lines and is the only one added, so the backfill next sprint can be smaller. I didn't run the full project suite, since `test_money.py` is the only test file I found.\n\nNext step: commit on a branch and open the PR, or leave it for your tech lead to review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":23049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f2bd4c5-13ed-472b-9fef-60d50ad57425","uuid":"1a00e18b-e0cf-4905-ba20-5cc7fbc3d333","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:39:50.421Z","request_id":"req_011CggKpJuuxJ2